# Build-context trim. Both app images and the bench images COPY a few explicit
# paths, but the *context* is whatever the daemon receives — without this, every
# `docker build` ships node_modules (159 MB) and the Locust venv (101 MB) to the
# daemon and then throws them away. Only things no image needs are listed here:
# trimming a directory that an image copies would break the `COPY` instead.
node_modules
**/node_modules
stress/locust/.venv
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore

dist
build
**/dist
**/build
coverage
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.vite
